Test is about 3 A's

@Annotation are used with methods
@BeforeSuite
@BeforeTest     : This annotation gets executed before @BeforeClass annotation and that too once
@BeforeClass    : This annotation gets executed before @BeforeMethod annotation and that too once
@BeforeMethod   : This annotation gets executed before every test case with @Test annotation
@Test           : This annotation represents the test case
@AfterMethod    : This annotation gets executed after every test case with @Test annotation
@AfterClass     : This annotation gets executed After @AfterMethod annotation and that too once
@AfterTest      : This annotation gets executed After @AfterClass annotation and that too once
@AfterSuite
-----------
@DataProvider
@Parameters

Attributes are used with annotations
Priority          : This is used to set the order of execution of test cases
Enabled           : This is responsible for setting if we want to execute a test case or not
dependsOnMethods  : This is used to set dependency clause b/w two methods
alwaysRun         : This will always run, no matter what
groups            : This is used to group the test cases
dependsOnGroups   : This will execute only if all the test case of a group mentioned is passed, else this will be ignored
timeOut           :

Test cases are executed in alphabetical order, this is the default execution mode of testNG

Assertions are used to validate the test cases
assertTrue
assertFalse
asserEquals
assertNotEquals
Hard Assertions Vs Soft Assertions